---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Ted McCormick - Software Developer / DevOps Engineer / Cloud Architect"
			description="This is the personal homepage and/or professional website for Edward C. 'Ted' McCormick, a software developer, DevOps Engineer, and Cloud Architect."
		/>
	</head>
	<body class="min-h-screen">
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-center items-center max-w-7xl xl:mx-auto">
				<div class="md:hidden">
					<h1 class="text-4xl text-blue-900">Hi there, my name is Ted.</h1>
				</div>
				<div class="m-4 w-96 box-content flex-none">
					<img class="object-none rounded-lg" src="/img/tedProfilePicture.jpg" alt="A profile picture of Edward C. &quotTed&quot McCormick" />
				</div>
				<div class="m-1 p-6 text-center md:text-left flex-1">
					<h1 class="text-4xl hidden md:inline text-blue-900">Hi there, my name is Ted.</h1>
					<h2 class="text-lg">I don't make software.</h2>
					<p>I make the infrastructure and tools that make the software your developers make better.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="w-100 m-4">
				<br />
				<p class="m-4 p-4">
					You can take a look at projects I've worked on and my resume above, or click through below to learn a
					little more about me and my background.
				</p>
				<br />
				<div
					class="flex flex-col p-6 m-4 md:p-0 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:gap-3 sm:grid md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 md:gap-6 mx-auto container w-screen sm:min-h-[200vh] lg:min-h-screen grid-flow-row auto-rows-fr"
				>
					<div
						id="dexter"
						class="col-span-1 mb-6 text-center min-h-screen sm:min-h-0 bg-cover rounded-lg bg-center"
						style="background-image: url(/img/Dexter_TownHall.JPG)"
						x-data="{ open: false }"
						@click.self="open = ! open"
						data-toggle="tooltip"
						data-placement="top"
						title="This is where I was born and raised. Almost literally - this building used to be the town library before it was repurposed into City Hall, and I spent a *lot* of time there growing up."
						alt="The City Administrative building of Dexter, Missouri, with a flag flying in front of it."
					>
						<div class="backdrop-blur-sm bg-white/60 w-full h-full min-h-screen sm:min-h-full" x-cloak x-show="open" x-transition @click="open = ! open">
							<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Dexter, Missouri</h3>
							<p class="text-base my-2">
								I was born in southeastern Missouri, and raised there from the time that I was six years old.
								It's great to grow up in a small town, and Dexter still has a total population of about 7,000.
								When I visited my friend on the 'wrong side of the tracks' (yes, there was literally a railroad
								track through Dexter, and there was a 'wrong' side!) my Mom got a call <i>before I got home.</i>
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div
						id="usnagrad"
						class="col-span-1 mb-6 text-center min-h-screen sm:min-h-0 bg-cover rounded-lg bg-center"
						style="background-image: url(/img/AnnapolisGraduationcropped.jpg)"
						x-data="{ open: false }"
						@click.self="open = ! open"
						aria-label="US Naval Academy Midshipmen Celebrating at Graduation in 2006 by throwing their hats in the air"
						data-toggle="tooltip"
						data-placement="top"
						title="Unfortunately, none of these people are me. I was too busy celebrating to take a picture."
						alt="Midshipmen of the US Naval Academy throwing their hats (covers) in the air at graduation."
					>
						<div class="backdrop-blur-sm bg-white/60 w-full h-full min-h-screen sm:min-h-full" x-cloak x-show="open" x-transition @click="open = ! open">
							<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">US Naval Academy<br />Annapolis, MD</h3>
							<p class="text-base my-2">
								I spent four years "by the Bay". I learned a lot - both about myself, during Plebe year, and
								what I was capable of surviving and thriving in, and also literally - I graduated with a
								Bachelor's of Science degree, even though my major was in Political Science. How many Poli-Sci
								majors do you know with two years of Calculus, and a year each of Electrical Engineering,
								Physics, and Chemistry?
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div
						id="swo"
						class="col-span-1 mb-6 text-center min-h-screen sm:min-h-0 bg-cover rounded-lg bg-center"
						style="background-image: url(/img/USS-Mahan.jpg)"
						x-data="{ open: false }"
						@click.self="open = ! open"
						aria-label="information goes here!"
						data-toggle="tooltip"
						data-placement="top"
						title="I'm actually in this picture! Behind 1/2 inch of steel plate, standing watch in the Combat Information Center."
						alt="USS Mahan, an Arleigh Burke class destroyer, returns to Norfolk, Virginia, after a deployment."
					>
						<div class="backdrop-blur-sm bg-white/60 w-full h-full min-h-screen sm:min-h-full" x-cloak x-show="open" x-transition @click="open = ! open">
							<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Surface Warfare Officer</h3>
							<p class="text-base my-2">
								I was in the US Navy for six years as a Surface Warfare Officer; part of that time as an
								engineering Officer, part of that as Training Officer, and did two deployments to the
								Mediterranean and off Somalia doing Counter-Piracy.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div
						id="family"
						class="col-span-1 mb-6 text-center min-h-screen sm:min-h-0 bg-cover rounded-lg bg-center"
						style="background-image: url(/img/family.jpg)"
						x-data="{ open: false }"
						@click.self="open = ! open"
						aria-label="Ted and his family after his daughter's violin recital, standing in front of skysrapers in downtown San Antonio, TX."
						data-toggle="tooltip"
						data-placement="top"
						title="Me, my beautiful wife, and our two amazing kids."
						alt="A picture of Ted McCormick, his wife, and two kids in front of skyscrapers in downtown San Antonio."
					>
						<div class="backdrop-blur-sm bg-white/60 w-full h-full min-h-screen sm:min-h-full" x-cloak x-show="open" x-transition @click="open = ! open">
							<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Family Life</h3>
							<p class="text-base my-2">
								I got out of the Navy to marry my wonderful wife. We settled in San Antonio because, well, if
								you want to become a Texan, marry a Texan!<br />
								My kids are <strong>awesome</strong>. Hectic, occasionally, but always awesome.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div
						id="codeup"
						class="col-span-1 mb-6 text-center min-h-screen sm:min-h-0 bg-cover rounded-lg bg-center"
						style="background-image: url(/img/codeup.jpg)"
						x-data="{ open: false }"
						@click.self="open = ! open"
						aria-label="The entrance and sign of Codeup, the coding bootcamp in San Antonio, TX, and Dallas, TX."
						data-toggle="tooltip"
						data-placement="top"
						title="Confession - I've been into Codeup's San Antonio campus one time - to interview. But a picture of a Zoom call is less interesting."
						alt="A view of the sign and door to Codeup, a coding bootcamp. This is the San Antonio, Texas, location."
					>
						<div class="backdrop-blur-sm bg-white/60 w-full h-full min-h-screen sm:min-h-full" x-cloak x-show="open" x-transition @click="open = ! open">
							<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Codeup</h3>
							<p class="text-base my-2">
								I joined Codeup in November of 2020, while everyone (and everything) was still remote from
								Covid, and graduated in May of '21.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div
						id="devops"
						class="col-span-2 mb-6 text-center order-last md:col-span-3 lg:order-none lg:col-span-2 min-h-screen sm:min-h-0 bg-contain rounded-lg bg-center bg-no-repeat"
						style="background-image: url(/img/devops-infinity.png)"
						x-data="{ open: false }"
						@click.self="open = ! open"
						aria-label="The DevOps continuous deployment infinity logo, representing the continuous integration/continuous deployment cycle."
						data-toggle="tooltip"
						data-placement="top"
						title="We all know why you're here!"
						alt="The DevOps infinite logo, showing the cycle of development/deployment/monitoring for software development."
					>
						<div class="backdrop-blur-sm bg-white/60 w-full h-full min-h-screen sm:min-h-full" x-cloak x-show="open" x-transition @click="open = ! open">
							<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">DevOps</h3>
							<p class="text-base my-2">
								Like most DevOps engineers (I think?) I've developed an eclectic set of skills - everything from
								basic automation and quality-of-life improvements through architecting cloud solutions,
								including implementing a zero-downtime, blue/green deployment architecture on one of SWBC's
								most busy serverless applications.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div
						id="swbc"
						class="col-span-1 mb-6 text-center min-h-screen sm:min-h-0 bg-cover rounded-lg bg-center"
						style="background-image: url(/img/swbc_lg.jpg)"
						x-data="{ open: false }"
						@click.self="open = ! open"
						aria-label="The headquarters building of Southwestern Business Corporation in San Antonio, TX, on a clear, sunny day."
						data-toggle="tooltip"
						data-placement="top"
						title="I've been to the Home Office exactly once. It was, and I'm not kidding, to return 'The Phoenix Project' to the Corporate Library. Yes, it was overdue!"
						alt="The headquarters building of Southwestern Business Corporation in San Antonio, TX, on a clear, sunny day."
					>
						<div class="backdrop-blur-sm bg-white/60 w-full h-full min-h-screen sm:min-h-full" x-cloak x-show="open" x-transition @click="open = ! open">
							<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">SWBC</h3>
							<p class="text-base my-2">
								I'll always be grateful to SWBC for letting me start my career as a DevOps Engineer. I've been
								there two years, and I've learned so much (and only brought down production once!).
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
